ages/2026/9/14/16x9.jpg"><media:title>WVU announces the 2026 tennis fall tournament schedule</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/16x9.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:02:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>15</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59392</s:story_id></item><item><title>Pozos Named Student-Athlete of the Week</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/14/mens-soccer-pozos-named-student-athlete-of-the-week</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/14/mens-soccer-pozos-named-student-athlete-of-the-week</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Pablo Pozos celebrates following a goal against George Mason" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/14/9-7half2goal1-4.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – West Virginia University men's soccer senior forward Pablo Pozos has been named the WVU Student-Athlete of the Week after tallying eight points in two wins for the Mountaineers.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/9-7half2goal1-4.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/9-7half2goal1-4.jpg"><media:title>Pablo Pozos celebrates following a goal against George Mason</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/9-7half2goal1-4.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:13:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59391</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers in the NFL – Week 1</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/14/football-mountaineers-in-the-nfl-week-1</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/14/football-mountaineers-in-the-nfl-week-1</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Austin Brinkman blocks a player in an NFL game against Denver" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/14/austin-brinkman1.jpg" /><br /><br />In Week 1 of the 2026 NFL season, eight former Mountaineers saw action. Four former players in Geno Smith, Zach Frazier, Dante Stills and Colton McKivitz started for their respective teams.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/austin-brinkman1.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/austin-brinkman1.jpg"><media:title>Austin Brinkman blocks a player in an NFL game against Denver</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/austin-brinkman1.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59394</s:story_id></item><item><title>New Premium Seating and Press Box Tower Announced for 2028</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/14/football-new-premium-seating-and-press-box-tower-announced-for-2028</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/14/football-new-premium-seating-and-press-box-tower-announced-for-2028</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="The new West Tower coming to Milan Puskar Stadium in 2028." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/14/WVU_WestTowerCoverImage.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Designed to elevate the college football fan experience, West Virginia University's Department of Intercollegiate Athletics has formally released information on the construction of a new premium seating tower and press box on the west side of Milan Puskar Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/WVU_WestTowerCoverImage.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/WVU_WestTowerCoverImage.jpg"><media:title>The new West Tower coming to Milan Puskar Stadium in 2028.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/14/WVU_WestTowerCoverImage.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59390</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Tie UConn to Cap Nonconference Slate</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/13/womens-soccer-mountaineers-tie-uconn-to-cap-nonconference-slate</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/13/womens-soccer-mountaineers-tie-uconn-to-cap-nonconference-slate</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Layla Thompson dribbles the ball during a game at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/13/3-EEN03160.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 8-ranked West Virginia University women's soccer team played to a 1-1 draw with UConn to cap its nonconference slate at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium in Morgantown on Sunday afternoon.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/13/3-EEN03160.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/13/3-EEN03160.jpg"><media:title>Layla Thompson dribbles the ball during a game at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/13/3-EEN03160.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:12:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59389</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Improve to 2-0 for First Time Since 2018</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/12/football-mountaineers-improve-to-2-0-for-first-time-since-2018</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/12/football-mountaineers-improve-to-2-0-for-first-time-since-2018</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="DJ Epps catches a 53-yard touchdown pass from Michael Hawkins in the first quarter of West Virginia's game against UT Martin at Milan Puskar Stadium in Morgantown, West Virginia" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/12/Epps-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – West Virginia used big plays from its offense to dispose of UT Martin 52-7 on Saturday afternoon before 47,049 sun-drenched spectators at Milan Puskar Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/12/Epps-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/12/Epps-Main.jpg"><media:title>DJ Epps catches a 53-yard touchdown pass from Michael Hawkins in the first quarter of West Virginia's game against UT Martin at Milan Puskar Stadium in Morgantown, West Virginia</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/12/Epps-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:26:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59388</s:story_id></item><item><title>FINAL: West Virginia Routs UT Martin, 52-7</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/12/football-game-day-west-virginia-hosts-ut-martin-on-family-day</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/12/football-game-day-west-virginia-hosts-ut-martin-on-family-day</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Two players celebrate after scoring a touchdown against UT Martin at Milan Puskar Stadium on Sept. 12, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/12/_DSC9769.jpeg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.VA — West Virginia defeated UT Martin, 52-7, to improve to 2-0 for the first time since 2018 at Milan Puskar Stadium in Morgantown, W.Va., on Sept. 12, 2026.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/12/_DSC9769.jpeg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/12/_DSC9769.jpeg"><media:title>Two players celebrate after scoring a touchdown against UT Martin at Milan Puskar Stadium on Sept. 12, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/12/_DSC9769.jpeg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 11:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59383</s:story_id></item></channel></rss>